  recipeId: sensor
  concept: 'Authored objective: Repair three independent sensor faults.

    Authored
    requirement: Repair the radar PLL, GNSS A feed and IMU B reference. Requalify
    after each repair.

    General teaching principle: Sensor outputs require proper
    calibration, reference and freshness before they can support a diagnosis.

    Only
    fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A measuring ruler is useful only if zero and units are correctly established.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: An old, uncalibrated or missing sensor reading is not reliable evidence.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Repair three independent sensor faults\u2019,
    which component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement
    should you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Repair three independent sensor faults\u2019, what result
    or observation would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish
    a predicted result from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 122, perform the objective \u2018Repair three independent sensor
    faults\u2019 in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Repair
    the radar PLL, GNSS A feed and IMU B reference. Requalify after each repair.\nThe
    mission evaluator decides completion; this tutorial does not grade your answer."
